A World and its inner Item hold each other twice: World.foo and the list World.items hold the Item, whose outer reference holds the World (four objects with the list and its array). The runtime frees an object and its inner object when they hold each other directly, not a ring through a collection; a collector would free it. The test's own cycle (PLAN.md "Who answers a cycle", rule 1); the compiler does not warn of an inner object that adds itself to a collection of its outer one yet.
